1. It's a creational design pattern
2. Used to create a copy of the object.

The idea is to not make another copy of object instead re-use the existing as creation
is a costly process.
Saves cost, resource and time.

use the clone() method.
For making a class as clonable we will implement the class using Clonable interface.
It's a marker interface which tells we can clone objects.


Deep copy vs shallow copy

In shallow copy: Primitive values are copied reference are not.
In deep copy: We need to override the clone method. References are also copied.






